{
 "name": "slot_pivot_4wd_chain",
 "description": "Slot-pivot 4WD: one M motor drives the front axle (8T->24T); a chain couples the rear axle 1:1, so all four\ntyres drive at the same speed (solid axles).  A free-rolling vertical post hangs into the 104 mm slot between the\nlanes: it guides the car along lane A, catches on the tilted plate's front edge, and the car - all four tyres\npushing - pivots round it onto lane B, where the post guides it again.  No steering and no timing: the battery\nlevel only changes the speed.",
